@base <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/alignment/design> .

<https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/alignment/design> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/design> ;
    dc:title "OntoGSN Alignments - the record"@en ;
    dc:creator "Tomas Bueno Momčilović"@en ;
    dc:publisher "https://www.fortiss.org/"@en ;
    dc:description """Why each axiom of https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/alignment exists, and why the correspondences
that were considered and rejected are absent.

The gsndesign: vocabulary supplies the backbone, so the SPARQL in development/design/README.md works over
this record unchanged. Four terms are added below because gsndesign:SourcePassage and its
properties are scoped by definition to the GSN Community Standard v3, and the sources here are
ARGO's ontology, its first-order axiomatisation and its paper.

Not read by development/dev_tools/prov_check.py, which validates an explicit list of three files in development/design/.
Statement records here therefore carry no gsndesign:structuralKey: nothing recomputes it, and a key
nothing checks is a key that silently rots."""@en ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "gsnaligndesign" ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/alignment> , <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/design> .


#################################################################
#    Local vocabulary
#    Four terms. Everything else is reused from gsndesign:.
#################################################################

gsnaligndesign:CitedArtefact rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "cited artefact"@en ;
    skos:definition "A whole document or graph that this alignment rests on."@en ;
    skos:note "Distinct from gsndesign:GSNCommunityStandardV3, which is the single artefact the OntoGSN record cites. An alignment rests on at least two."@en .

gsnaligndesign:CitedPassage rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "cited passage"@en ;
    skos:definition "A quoted extract of a cited artefact, located within it."@en ;
    skos:note "Not gsndesign:SourcePassage: that class is defined as a passage of the GSN Community Standard v3, and gsndesign:quotedText, gsndesign:clause and gsndesign:pageRef all declare it as their domain. Reusing them here would type ARGO's text as part of the GSN standard."@en .

gsnaligndesign:passageText rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gsnaligndesign:CitedPassage ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "passage text"@en ;
    skos:definition "The extract, verbatim."@en .

gsnaligndesign:locator rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gsnaligndesign:CitedPassage ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "locator"@en ;
    skos:definition "Where the extract sits in its artefact: line range for a graph, section for a paper."@en ;
    skos:note "A line range is evidence, not identity - it moves when the file is re-saved. The passage text is what identifies the extract."@en .


