#################################################################
#    Decisions to represent nothing
#    Each of these is a correspondence that was considered and rejected. They generate no
#    statement; the reasoning is the record.
#################################################################

gsnaligndesign:dd-0019
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "A GSN solution is not mapped to an ARGO premise, and is left unmapped entirely."@en ;
    prov:used gsnaligndesign:src-0010 , gsnaligndesign:src-0011 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0015 ;
    skos:note "Consequence: a step supported only by evidence carries no ARGO premise. ARGO's requirement is existential, so this is not an inconsistency, but an ARGO query for the premises of a case returns claims and never evidence. Recorded in alignments/README.md."@en .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0020
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "The claim implicit in a solution's noun phrase is not minted as a bridge class."@en ;
    prov:used gsnaligndesign:src-0010 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0015 ;
    gsndesign:supersededBy gsnaligndesign:dd-0019 .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0021
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "No occurrent individuals are minted: neither the act of inferring behind a step nor the act of argument creation behind a case."@en ;
    prov:used gsnaligndesign:src-0009 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0016 .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0022
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "OntoGSN's boolean status decorators are not mapped to ARGO."@en ;
    prov:used gsnaligndesign:src-0013 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0017 ;
    skos:note "Applies to gsn:true, gsn:valid, gsn:defeated and gsn:inDoubt. ARGO has 24 fewer datatype properties than OntoGSN for a reason: it has none at all."@en ;
    gsndesign:mentionsTerm gsn:true , gsn:valid , gsn:defeated , gsn:inDoubt .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0023
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "gsn:Argument is not declared a subclass of argo:argument, in either direction."@en ;
    prov:used gsnaligndesign:src-0004 , gsnaligndesign:src-0005 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0010 ;
    skos:note "Forward, it collides with ARGO's exactly-one-conclusion restriction wherever a structure has more than one top goal, and does so silently by merging the two conclusions. Backward, it is false as a universal - an argument in a legal brief is not a GSN argument - and would impose GSN's mandatory single identifier on every ARGO argument. gsnalign:CaseArgument replaces both."@en ;
    gsndesign:mentionsTerm gsn:Argument .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0024
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "gsn:Justification is left unmapped."@en ;
    gsndesign:noSourceRecorded true ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0018 ;
    skos:note "A justification is a Toulmin warrant - rationale for the inference rather than a premise of it. ARGO's paper argues explicitly against the Toulmin model, so there is nothing to map onto, and modelling it as a premise would change what the case says."@en ;
    gsndesign:mentionsTerm gsn:Justification .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0025
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "GSN's packaging and notation classes are left unmapped."@en ;
    prov:used gsnaligndesign:src-0016 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0018 ;
    skos:note "Covers AssuranceCase, Artefact, Module, View, Catalogue, Pattern, Template, InstantiationDataReference, away elements, contracts and assurance claim points. Worth noting that ARGO's paper recommends treating argument schemes as instances of a class under ICE, which is the shape gsn:Pattern and gsn:instantiationOf already have - but the agreement is methodological and there is no ARGO term to point at."@en ;
    gsndesign:mentionsTerm gsn:AssuranceCase , gsn:Artefact , gsn:Module , gsn:Pattern .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0026
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "No SHACL shapes are written for the alignment layer."@en ;
    gsndesign:noSourceRecorded true ;
    gsndesign:noRationaleRecorded true .

gsnaligndesign:dd-0027
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:NoFormalism ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "The derivation rules that would populate the bridge classes are specified but not implemented."@en ;
    gsndesign:noSourceRecorded true ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsnaligndesign:why-0020 ;
    skos:note "The nine rules are tabulated in alignments/README.md. Without them the alignment is a TBox only: it states what the correspondence is, and mints nothing."@en .
